17] [17592186442429 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442429 #edb/ref 1071 "$(-6)\\cdot (-4)\\cdot 2=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442429 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "515d2e58-90d5-54f6-8477-014fb0487556" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442429 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by multiplying the first two numbers. We have the product of two negatives, which gives a positive:\n\n$$\n(-6)\\cdot (-4)=24\n$$\n\nSo we now have\n\n$$\n{{(-6)\\cdot (-4)}_{⏟}}_{24}\\cdot 2=24\\cdot 2.\n$$\n\nThen, we work out this remaining product using the fact that the product of two positives gives a positive:\n\n$$\n24\\cdot 2=48\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442430 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442430 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128409" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442430 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442430 #edb/ref 1071 "$7\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-5)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442430 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6db7b1f8-571b-596f-b937-087002cb4535" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442430 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by multiplying the first two numbers. We have the product of a positive and a negative, which gives a negative:\n\n$$\n7\\cdot (-2)=-14\n$$\n\nSo we now have\n\n$$\n{{7\\cdot (-2)}_{⏟}}_{-14}\\cdot (-5)=(-14)\\cdot (-5).\n$$\n\nThen, we work out this remaining product using the fact that the product of two negatives gives a positive:\n\n$$\n(-14)\\cdot (-5)=14\\cdot 5=70\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442431 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442406 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442431 #edb/ref 1069 "q-180928" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442431 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442431 #edb/ref 1071 "$(-3.1)\\cdot 7.3=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442431 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6e4f8c55-ff7a-58f7-9342-3b5b8d2c1065" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442431 #edb/ref 1074 "We have the product of