1 "$(-2)\\cdot (-9)=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442434 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bebcf13b-8bc8-52b9-bfbb-3d010d1e3235" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442434 #edb/ref 1074 "We have a product of two negative numbers, $-2$ and $-9.$ So the product will be positive:\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot (-9)=\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $2$ and $9$ without any signs: $2\\cdot 9=18.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot (-9)=18.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442435 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442435 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42994" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442435 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442435 #edb/ref 1071 "$(-\\frac{7}{3})\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442435 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c193a4aa-2a3b-50a7-9351-eac6230e1fa9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442435 #edb/ref 1074 "We have a product of a negative number and a positive number, so the product will be negative:\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{7}{3})\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}=-(\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{4})\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply the fractions by multiplying the numerators and denominators separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}) & =-(\\frac{7\\cdot 5}{3\\cdot 4}) \\\\  & =-(\\frac{35}{12}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{35}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442436 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442436 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128394" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442436 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442436 #edb/ref 1071 "$(-7)\\cdot (-3)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442436 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c2277e51-aeb9-59a4-9f7f-011ebd2053af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442436 #edb/ref 1074 "We have a product of two negative numbers, $-7$ and $-3.$ So the product will be positive:\n\n$$\n(-7)\\cdot (-3)=\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $7$ and $3$ without any signs: $7\\cdot 3=21.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n(-7)\\cdot (-3)=21.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442437 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442437 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128424" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442437 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442437 #edb/ref 1071 "$2.2\\cdot (-4.5)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442437 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c5da7489-1e96-592e-8ffe-aaecfa0d4fb2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442437 #edb/ref 1074 "We have the product of a positive number and a negative number, which gives a negative number.\n\n$$\n2.2\\cdot (-4.5)=-(2.2\\cdot 4.5)=-9.9\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442438 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442415 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442438 #edb/ref 1069 "q-180551" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442438 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442438 #edb/ref 1071 "$5\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 2=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442438 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dcae9997-c063-556b-b99d-bfc224ab7e6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442438 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by multiplying the first two numbers. We have the product of a positive and a negative, which gives a negative:\n\n$$\n5\\cdot (-3)=-15\n$$\n\nSo we now have\n\n$$\n{{5\\cdot (-3)}_{⏟}}_{-15}\\cdot 2=(-15)\\cdot 2.\n$$\n\nThen, we work out this remaining product using the fact that a negative times a positive gives a negative:\n\n$$\n(-15)\\cdot 2=-(15\\cdot 2)=-30\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442439 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442439 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128408" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442439 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442439 #edb/ref 1071 "$(-4)\\cdot (-4)\\cdot (-3)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442439 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "edd9589d-5442-58a3-84f8-fb0a90d9d945" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442439 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by multiplying the first two numbers. We have the product of two negatives, which gives a positive: \n\n$$\n(-4)\\cdot (-4)=16\n$$\n\nSo we now have\n\n$$\n{{(-4)\\cdot (-4)}_{⏟}}_{16}\\cdot (-3)=16\\cdot (-3).\n$$\n\nThen, we work out this remaining product using the fact that a positive times a negative gives a negative:\n\n$$\n16\\cdot (-3)=-(16\\cdot 3)=-48\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442440 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442440 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128430" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442440 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442440 #edb/ref 1071 "$(-1.6)\\cdot (-4.3)=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442440 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f9693f01-1b7b-566f-8d4a-ee5e7f15cd38" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442440 #edb/ref 1074 "We have the product of two negative numbers, which gives a positive number.\n\n$$\n(-1.6)\\cdot (-4.3)=1.6\\cdot 4.3=6.88.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
